# DEMIURGE core layout — kernel cmdline change. APPLY BY HAND, AT THE BENCH,
# NEVER DURING A PERFORMANCE. EMGOR owns /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt. Needs reboot.
#
# cmdline.txt is ONE line. Replace the existing `isolcpus=3` token with:
#
#   isolcpus=1-3
#
# (keep threadirqs usbcore.autosuspend=-1; leave nohz_full/rcu_nocbs alone —
# stock kernel rejects them, see cmdline.txt.additions. If you ever run a
# CONFIG_NO_HZ_FULL kernel, mirror them to 1-3.)
#
# Optional, flagged UNVERIFIED on this kernel: isolcpus=domain,managed_irq,1-3
# (managed_irq keeps managed IRQs off the isolated cores). Try only if
# /proc/interrupts shows IRQs on cores 1-3 after demiurge-irq-isolate.
#
# Companions that must change in the same session (see docs/core-layout.md):
#   - demiurge-irq-isolate.sh: MASK_HEX=7 -> 1, MASK_LIST=0-2 -> 0   (IRQs to core 0 only)
#   - demiurge.service.d: CPUAffinity=0-2 -> 0 (keep AllowedCPUs=0-3)
#   - demiurge-power low mode keeps only 3 cores online (0,ISO,1) and would
#     offline a core this map needs: do not use power=low with this layout.
#
# Verify after reboot:
#   cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/isolated      # 1-3
